This commit fixes multiple issues in the paging failure handling implementation
and ensures proper session cleanup and HSS notification.

Fixed Issues:
1. Build error: Variable name collision (mme_self) in mme-timer.c
2. Missing Purge-UE-Request transmission to HSS on paging failure
3. Crash due to NULL enb_ue assertion in mme_gtp_send_delete_session_request
4. FSM crash when directly removing UE context after paging failure

Key Changes:
- src/mme/mme-timer.c: Renamed variable to avoid collision with function name
- src/mme/mme-context.c: Added paging_failure_policy configuration loading with logs
- src/mme/mme-gtp-path.c: Handle NULL enb_ue case for paging failure scenarios
- src/mme/mme-path.c: Add Purge-UE-Request transmission and proper FSM cleanup
- src/mme/emm-sm.c: Transition to exception state when no sessions remain
- configs/open5gs/mme.yaml.in: Add paging_failure_policy configuration option

3GPP Compliance:
Implements 3GPP TS 29.272 Section 7.2.14 (Purge UE) requirement to send
Purge-UE-Request to HSS when MME deletes UE context after paging failure.

Testing:
Verified on 2025-10-15 at 18:29:34 - no crashes, proper Purge-UE-Request
transmission, and successful session deletion on paging failure.

